a gun-toting asgardian a sassy skeleton  weird wigs oil wrestling and bizarre 90s  sitcom parodies what other weird moments  do you remember from xena warrior  princess  it isn't uncommon these days for show  runners and filmmakers to reward fans  for paying careful attention to the end  credits adding hidden details is a  terrific strategy for getting the fandom  together and giving them something to  look for it also creates buzz in online  communities over the latest new treasure  hiding in something as mundane as a  title card or an ongoing credits gag  xena warrior princess was a pioneer in  this realm messages and episodes were so  subtle that even some of the more  attentive fans missed them the first  time around but thanks to the magic of  dvds and streaming video eager fans can  now hit pause during the show's end  credits to find an amusing disclaimer  hidden at the end of most episodes from  ensuring viewers that no mythical  creatures were harmed during the  production of the episode to praising  danny kay's the court jester these silly  disclaimers are a reminder that xena  never took itself too seriously and  viewers shouldn't either  one of the things that made xena special  was the show's ability to balance  serious drama and powerful writing with  plenty of goofy hijinks to lighten up  the mood of all the show's shenanigans  and amusing anachronisms few are more  absurdly wacky than the series odd  mashup of goldie hawn and kurt russell's  1987 film overboard and the fox series  married with children married with fish  sticks had an amnesiac gabrielle duped  by divorce merman hagar into believing  she was the mother of his out of control  brood to make things extra loony the  oceanic parallel world was rife with  doppelgangers from gabby's real life  plagued with strange and surreal horrors  like bad fashion catty neighbors and a  misogynistic husband gabby's new reality  was a nightmare but it was their three  out of control offspring that kept  viewers up at night wondering what  they'd seen unable to get those images  out of their heads in order from oldest  to youngest gabrielle met three children  straight out of special effects  purgatory walrus boy flipper mini hell  priest urchin and the octopus adjacent  baby roe at once horrifying and weirdly  cute roe was one of the most puzzling  creatures dreamed up by xena creators  the meme potential alone garners plenty  of pauses among viewers today  salon writer andrew leonard was spot on  when he called the xena halloween  episode girls just want to have fun the  disco-lesbian vampire episode starring a  lord darkness from legend lookalike as  bacchus the episode had a little  something for everyone there was a dance  party possessed wolves and a random  musician's disembodied but still  completely animated head attached to  everything from pikes to scarecrows the  production team got so carried away with  all of this crazy music video energy  that they even forgot to edit out a  propane tank which can be seen in all  its anachronistic glory but it's the  super sultry vampire lust in this  episode that solidified its place in the  annals of tv thurstom helping shape the  show's image as an iconic lesbian love  story since vampirism has always been  used as a metaphor for sexuality the  show's creators decided to use the  bakaye as a pre-hellenic stand-in for  vampires it let them sneakily explore  gabrielle and xena's sexuality in a way  that wasn't standard for the era  director tj scott told xena magazine  that he and lucy lawless set out to push  the envelope in terms of sexual content  the result was a super hot scene with  gotheed out gabby and xena lost in  erotic vamp bliss  some xena warrior princess story arcs  are darker than others such as the  altitail once a siberian amazon alti was  booted by her tribe when she became a  power hungry shaman she would go on to  become a toxic frenemy to a still evil  xena she worked to manipulate the young  chakram wielder into murdering the  entire amazon tribe under the promise  the shaman would make xena a destroyer  of nations this is war zener  just a little one  although xena would live up to this  title alti failed to tell her it came  with a curse the dark shaman placed the  curse on her lover barias and unborn son  solon costing barias his life and solon  his parents if that super heavy  backstory wasn't enough it got even  darker eventually a reformed xena  journeyed with the northern amazons to  the amazon resting place there she was  forced to confront the skeletons of the  amazons she once killed in the name of  power but in the midst of this dark  moment if you look carefully you'll see  one sassy skeleton flipping the bird in  its final moments  there are countless reasons to love carl  urban if you're paying close attention  he's everywhere he looked majestic as  heck in his fair garb and glorious  golden locks as eomer in the lord of the  rings as a super salty but sweet bones  he's a bright spot in the oft divisive  j.j abrams star trek films he pops up in  thor ragnarok as scourge he even had a  star wars cameo these days he can be  found in his breakthrough role as billy  butcher on the boys of course xena fans  have been on team urban since the late  90s when he first appeared on both xena  and hercules the legendary journeys  urban's appearance on the two shows were  some of his earliest roles and he didn't  miss a chance to display his acting  chops on xena he showed up in four  different roles often looking barely  recognizable thanks to the magic of a  great hair and makeup department he  first appeared as mael a psychopathic  ancient greek version of the biblical  isaac's half-brother urban later spent  eight episodes as zena's handsome lover  and murderer julius caesar he then took  on more of a comic role donning wings  and bleached hair as aphrodite's son  cupid finally he played a stone age  cannibal named core alongside selma  blair in lifeblood an episode that was  meant to be a backdoor pilot for the  scrapped series amazon high  like carl urban gina torres is one of  those actors that keeps taking roles in  iconic series that sci-fi fans fall in  love with long before her appearance on  hercules and xena torres had been  building a reputation as a solid  television and film actor and post xena  she continued with roles on firefly  angel and westworld to name a few most  recently she can be found as a main cast  member on 9-1-1 lone star where she  plays emt tommy vega fans of torres  watching xena warrior princess for the  first time will be thrilled when she  turns up as the perfectly eyelinered  cleopatra in the king of assassins yet  another doppelganger episode it places  cleopatra jockster atollicus gabrielle  and xena in the middle of fresh mistaken  identity mayhem courtesy of jockster's  much cooler evil twin jet while much of  the episode revolves around thwarting a  plot to kill cleo there's a whole thing  going on between the queen of egypt and  our favorite king of thieves it's  complete with a steamy bathtub scene and  enough double entendres to fill a trojan  horse  back in the 1990s lgbtq representation  was rare and typically poorly executed  in the 90s every time anyone or anything  dared to be out and proud some people  really lost their minds over it it was  also a time when tv producers had even  less autonomy when it came to their  production and writing decisions than  they do today from the show's beginning  the network was aware of the possibility  that the relationship between gabby and  xena could be perceived as romantic so  they went out of their way to forbid any  clear-cut lesbian relationship but what  about subtext as it turns out the  network was fine with lgbtq subtext  especially since it became clear pretty  quickly that the subtext was part of  what fans kept coming back to see found  it  ah  i found it  [Applause]  i learned from the best  audiences ended up with plenty of steamy  scenes where the heroes were bathing  together washing each other's backs and  having heartfelt conversations about how  they couldn't live without each other  for those of us who lived to see those  super shippable moments there were  plenty of opportunities to hit the pause  button there are goodbye kisses like in  the episode the return of kalisto there  are substitute body kisses like when  xena kisses gabby and atella kiss's body  there are four head kisses cheek kisses  life-saving kisses and gothy vampire  kisses and every one of them looks great  as smartphone wallpaper  anyone who writes or reads fanfiction  knows that some fantasies are better  kept private a lesson jockster learns  the hard way in the quill is mightier  see while xena and gabrielle were  forging a bond that would last for  eternity their goofy friend joxer was  not so secretly holding a torch for  gabrielle one of the great things about  joxer's relationship with the heroes is  that no matter how knee deep and cringe  he was at all times xena and gabrielle  always loved and respected him they even  had empathy for his feelings about gabby  nonetheless he could be incredibly  annoying and he never seemed to tire of  pushing the limits of the girl's  tolerance but when aphrodite suddenly  gifted gabrielle the power to write her  reality mayhem ensued after conjuring  and obsessively fishing xena and some  various troubles for the gods gaby got  the bright idea to have all the victims  of her writing sleep in a nearby cave  until she could work out a solution amid  the mess a bad attempt at love poetry  manifested jockster's gabby fantasies as  three naked dancing gabrielles thanks to  some fun camera work the scene remained  fairly g-rated but it still became one  of the silliest sites in the entire  series if only all bad writing was so  innocuous  generally speaking big budget films and  higher caliber tv shows will go out of  their way to conceal stunt doubles other  entertainment options don't seem to be  terribly concerned perhaps it's because  the director is confident the scenes  will go so fast or their audience will  be so dazzled by their sleight of hand  that they won't look too closely or  perhaps they're just working with a  limited time frame and budget so they do  the best they can under those  constraints and move on to the next shot  but some productions just don't even  seem to care and not every actor can  have a near perfect photo double like  says from only murderers in the building  is that filler i'm over here  what the  what is this face off either way the  results can be pretty amusing when stunt  doubles are obvious and xena warrior  princess was a frequent offender this  was especially comical for a series that  spent so much time focusing on  doppelganger gags things seemed to go  off the rails at some point during  season 4 when blatant stunt doubles  became a common sight one good example  of this guaranteed to make you laugh is  when an obvious stunt double can be seen  riding argo in the episode end game  sooner or later everybody reaches the  breaking point where it's time to just  phone it in that seems to be exactly  what happened in if the shoe fits when  for no clear reason gabrielle  inexplicably had the most absurd wig in  one scene only in the episode a burlap  sack clad gabrielle tells a young  runaway princess her version of the  cinderella story starring herself as the  lovely and put upon tyrella throughout  the episode each of gabrielle's  companions take over storytelling at  some point with aphrodite jockster and  xena each giving it their own spin while  the story within a story featured some  pretty fancy wigs and costumes back in  real life gabrielle was still hanging  around in a burlap sack that's why it's  that much more puzzling when she's  randomly seen rifling through her  belongings while wearing a bizarrely  poofy much redder wig sometimes you just  have to work with what you've got on  hand so you can clock out in time for  happy hour  there are some episodes of xena that  beautifully capture the profound  complexity and depth of the human  experience touching the hearts and souls  of yours then there are the others  little problems begins with xena body  swapping with a little girl in a coma  and things only get worse from there  aphrodite and gabrielle are plotting to  steal some magic soul dividing oil from  club owners and skeezy conjoined twins  castor and pollux for some reason their  convoluted plan involves pretending to  be swedish conjoined twins and oil  wrestling the brothers to get into their  exclusive twins only club the episode is  all over the place but the nonsensical  scenes with gabrielle and aphrodite  pretending to be valkyrie twins are  worth the price of admission alone check  out one of our newest videos right here  plus even more looper videos about your  favorite tv shows are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

